<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee official to meet growers, exporters.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee official to meet growers, exporters.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of the primary commodities department in Brazil's Industry and Commerce Ministry, Mauricio Assis, is to hold two meetings this week with members of the private sector, traders said.</p>
<p>This afternoon Assis will talk about credit problems with officials from the National Coffee Council (CNC) which represents growers, said CNC secretary general Sergio Amaral.</p>
<p>On Oct 16, Assis will meet representatives from the Brazilian Coffee Exporters' Federation and the Brazilian Coffee Exporters' Association in a regular monthly session to discuss the progress of coffee exports, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
